text.paragraph:
RECTIV ointment is not for oral, ophthalmic, or intravaginal use.  Hands should be washed after application of the ointment [see 

                        Patient Instruction

                     ].

Administration of RECTIV is contraindicated in patients who are using a selective inhibitor of cyclic guanosine monophosphate (cGMP)-specific phosphodiesterase type 5 (PDE5), such as sildenafil, vardenafil, and tadalafil, as these are shown to potentiate the hypotensive effects of organic nitrates [see 
                           DRUG INTERACTIONS
                            (

                              7.1

                           )
                           ].

In rare cases, therapeutic doses of organic nitrates have caused methemoglobinemia [ see OVERDOSAGE (
10
) ] .

Advise patient not to use RECTIV with medications for erectile dysfunction such as Viagra (sildenafil), Levitra (vardenafil), and Cialis (tadalafil).  These products have been shown to increase the hypotensive effects of RECTIV and other nitrate drugs [see Contraindications (

                        4

                     )].
